From ucc1ef8c8158d6b73 at groups.google.com  Tue Jun 18 21:01:05 2013
From: ucc1ef8c8158d6b73 at groups.google.com (Yihui Xie)
Date: Tue, 18 Jun 2013 21:01:05 +0000
Subject: Re: How do I properly imbed an image URL in an HTML string
Message-ID: <ZKz1YT_UvSs.EsrI7KdeYBUJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <ZKz1YT_UvSs.P9VGwzXeFNIJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
References: <ZKz1YT_UvSs.P9VGwzXeFNIJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/ZKz1YT_UvSs/m/EsrI7KdeYBUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You can always base64 encode the images; see
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_URI_scheme

There are a number of ways to do this in R. You may see
markdown:::.b64EncodeImages for an example (note ::: is usually a red
flag, so use with care).

For shiny, I think an easier way is to register a resource path
prefix, e.g. you can put your images under the images/ directory, and

addResourcePath('images', file.path(getwd(), 'images'))

Then http://localhost:8100/images/FinalReportb2.PNG will work.

Regards,
Yihui
