The log files deleting themselves is expected; we do that when we detect the R process exiting normally after we asked nicely, so we don't fill up the hard drive with log files that don't tell us anything interesting.

Our servers are all Ubuntu as well, and I'm running Ubuntu 13.04. I don't see this problem normally but there have been times when we've had extra R processes hanging around seemingly forever, so I don't doubt what you're seeing. Can you try killing all the processes, and then deploying the simplest possible R app (like hello shiny <http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#hello-shiny>) and see if the problem reproduces with that?

